  "details": "I changed avatars and ended up accidentally into an error robot locally (attached screenshot) temporarily, until I switched to another avatar and back into the same avatar again and then the avatar loaded correctly. This issue repeated a day after, but only remotely to another user. Logs pointed to the above error.\n\nI've not been able to reproduce the issue in the past year, and I'm unable to reproduce this again. I don't have steps to reproduce this for this bug report to be actionable and I'm not sure where the problem lies either, unfortunately.\n\nAffected avatar: Comfy MoeFT Hush_Rush （lilToon） by WubTheCaptain (`avtr_5d925964-e921-4b24-81a9-f19eef7d3eb1`)\n\nThis is an eye-/facetracked avatar, with its FT parameters controlled via OSC with VRCFaceTracking 5.4.4.1, EyeTrackVR App 0.2.5.6 and Babble v2.0.7, animated on the avatar with animations (including eyes).\n\nWhat typically happens when this avatar's loading malfunctions: The avatar loads with eye-/facetracking parameters saved in \"on\" state, then based on a random chance the eye-/facetracking animations may freeze on avatar load until switching out/resetting the avatar. Rarely, VRCFaceTracking on the host PC may crash instead or require a restart. This is the first time it's given me an error robot instead in-app.",
